Bridge 0126 (G7): port of UniXNU/AdrenoMetal 243d63c bridge/patches/0011-two-plane-shadow-as-memory-lies.patch (MIT; by hand, its context
does not apply here). A two-plane surface texture's shadow image starts as its memory lies instead of zero-filled: its copy in writes every
texel before any command reads it, so the zero-fill was pure cost (most of a full-screen surface's making on a render server).
Knob: SWEET_M2V_TWO_PLANE_ZERO=1 restores the zero-fill (on by default: no zero-fill).

